      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Mennonite Tourist Church in Pinecraft has been a landmark since 1946, originally purchased for $7,500, equivalent to about $124,000 today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pinecraft%2C_Florida",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Amish from Indiana and Ohio commonly travel to Pinecraft on buses operated by Crossroad Tours and Pioneer Trails, available year-round except in June and July.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pinecraft%2C_Florida",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Pinecraft, Florida, is a popular winter vacation destination for many North American Amish and Mennonites, particularly from states like Indiana and Pennsylvania.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pinecraft%2C_Florida",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The transition from camps to residential areas in Pinecraft began in the early 1940s, with significant housing construction continuing through the 1950s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pinecraft%2C_Florida",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "In 1949, single lots in Pinecraft sold for $200, while corner lots were priced at $225, reflecting the area's early development.",
